Task 1.3: Wire the engine into WebAudio (Green)

What: startMusic/stopMusic now drive the pure MusicScheduler. Per-theme
gain buses carry the crossfade (fade-in on start/hand-off, fade-out on
stop with a short ramp so silence never clicks); a light 200ms pump
driver tops up the scheduler lookahead, while every note time comes
from the AudioContext clock (no setInterval timing loop, no drift).
The historical one-argument startMusic(settings) call sites keep
working via the default ROOM_THEME; settings are re-gated on every
pump so bedtime/mute still stop the music by themselves.

